WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.979 --> 00:00:06.609
President Trump has fashioned himself as one
of the decade's biggest villains in a confusing

00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:08.520
new campaign clip.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:13.370
The video – released by a Twitter account
called @TrumpWarRoom, which itself is reportedly

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:19.800
managed by the Trump 2020 campaign superimposes
Trump's grinning face onto footage of Thanos

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.269
in Avengers: Endgame during one of the villain's
final scenes.

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:29.240
In the clip, two different versions of Trump's
head admire Thanos' Infinity Gauntlet before

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.980
Brolin's voice utters, "I am inevitable."

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.610
Right after President Thanos' proclamation,
the video switches to a clip of Speaker of

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:42.210
the House Nancy Pelosi discussing the ongoing
Trump impeachment inquiry – only for her

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:46.430
and several other high-ranking Democrats to
promptly get "dusted."

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.480
Trump's team captioned the video,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.789
"House Democrats can push their sham impeachment
all they want.

00:00:52.789 --> 00:00:55.500
President Trump's re-election is inevitable."

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.789
This tweet comes on the heels of the announcement
that House Democrats will charge the President

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:05.930
with two articles of impeachment specifically,
"abuse of power and obstruction of Congress"

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:10.770
which, if it proceeds, would make Trump the
third sitting President in United States history

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.400
to face impeachment.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:17.930
All of this makes the video a pretty confusing
take on Trump's political future, and it leads

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:22.590
one to wonder whether or not Trump's team
has even seen Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:28.020
Firstly, there's the fact that Thanos is,
frankly, a genocidal maniac who kills his

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:33.160
adopted daughter for his own gain and decimates
half of the living creatures on Earth.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.180
Certainly, Trump's team wouldn't want to liken
the President to such a villainous character

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.540
if they're trying to get him re-elected.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.780
Secondly, the Endgame moment that follows
the one used in this campaign clip doesn't

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:46.420
exactly work out well for Thanos.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:51.240
Though the tweet makes it look like Trump-Thanos
is about to achieve victory, anyone who's

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:55.530
seen Endgame knows what really happens is
quite the opposite.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:02:00.100
It appears Trump's team may not have realized
this, which makes the depiction of Trump as

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.710
Thanos extra confusing.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.630
"He's pretty good at that.”

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:08.599
This isn't the first time that the President
and his team have used a super-popular piece

00:02:08.599 --> 00:02:12.810
of entertainment to push forward his 2020
re-election campaign.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:17.709
Back in April 2019 when the final season of
Game of Thrones was dominating the pop culture

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:23.500
landscape, Trump uploaded to his Twitter account
an image using Thrones' instantly recognizable

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.500
font.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:28.549
The photo showed the President's back with
the caption, "No collusion.

00:02:28.549 --> 00:02:29.549
No obstruction.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:33.719
For the haters and the radical left Democrats
— Game Over."

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:38.620
The meme arrived right after the redacted
Mueller report which documents the findings

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:43.819
of former U.S. Special Counsel Robert Mueller's
investigation into possible Russian interference

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:48.829
in the 2016 U.S. election, as well as other
allegations of obstruction of justice by President

00:02:48.829 --> 00:02:51.000
Trump first made the news.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.310
Game of Thrones' network HBO wasted no time
responding to Trump's tweet.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:58.060
In a statement released by Deadline, the network
replied,

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:02.530
"Though we can understand the enthusiasm for
Game of Thrones now that the final season

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:08.540
has arrived, we still prefer our intellectual
property not be used for political purposes."

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:13.280
This was HBO's most civil response to President
Trump to date.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:18.280
In November 2018, Trump used the Game of Thrones
font for an image that read "sanctions are

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:24.599
coming" in a clear, direct reference to Thrones'
famous tagline, "winter is coming" to which

00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:25.599
HBO cheekily tweeted,

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:28.829
"How do you say trademark misuse in Dothraki?"

00:03:28.829 --> 00:03:33.099
However, the President's Thrones references
were only getting started.

00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:38.310
In January 2019, Trump carried out the same
trick on his Instagram account, this time

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:42.090
noting that "the wall is coming" rather than
"sanctions."

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:46.029
Unsurprisingly, plenty of people weren't too
happy with that one either.

00:03:46.029 --> 00:03:51.640
This latest effort hasn't sparked any pushback
from Marvel just yet, but all in all, the

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:56.670
Trump-as-Thanos video sends a pretty muddled
message since Thanos isn't a sympathetic figure,

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:01.079
ends up losing Endgame's biggest battle, and
then dies.

00:04:01.079 --> 00:04:05.359
Even in these politically fraught times, most
people can probably agree that pop culture

00:04:05.359 --> 00:04:09.810
and politics should remain separate after
all, where can you escape the news if not

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:15.529
at a screening of a Marvel flick? but Trump's
latest attempt is definitely worth some discussion.

